{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/936407-expanding-mortal-magic","id":936407,"title":"Expanding Mortal Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-23T21:30:14-07:00","id":936407,"title":"Expanding Mortal Magic","content":"So, <i>any</i> mortal can abjure/banish/bind/summon/ward Ephemeral beings. Some are better at it (good rating in Resolve, Composure, Wits, and Occult), but anyone can with a soul can do it.<br /> <br /> What kind of &quot;generic&quot; rituals could be added to this list? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/717704-souls-are-a-disease\">I made a way to add souls to the list of things you can perform rituals against</a>, but I'm thinking more about stuff that <i>anyone</i> can do if they know it's possible.<br /> <br /> One thing would be to port the rules <i>directly</i> and let you use them against Horrors. Binding and Warding work if you replace Rank with Potency, but Abjuration would need some changes (Have it just scare them off on a Success?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:32:04-07:00","id":936408,"title":"","content":"Go buy a copy of Second Sight and take a look at the Thaumaturges chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:34:01-07:00","id":936409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/936407-expanding-mortal-magic?p=936408#post936408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go buy a copy of Second Sight and take a look at the Thaumaturges chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize, but I'm currently unemployed and staring at less than $500 in my bank account. Could you please give a summary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T03:51:21-07:00","id":936484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/936407-expanding-mortal-magic?p=936408#post936408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go buy a copy of Second Sight and take a look at the Thaumaturges chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that chapter provides what amechra wants, as a character needs the Thaumaturge minor template to be able to work those rituals, and the availability of that template is up to the storyteller.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there are more rituals in any book that any mortal can use, except for the idea that some mortals perform &quot;rituals&quot; to appease ephemeral beings so that the being grants what the mortal wants. But this is not actual magic, although the mortal might think so. It's more of a quid pro quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T08:48:09-07:00","id":936551,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturges from Second Sight are a minor template of magic users, divied up by magic tradition such as hermetic, shamanistic, folk witch, etc, since psychics in second edition are now people with supernatural merits, more than one person believes that thaumaturgy would/will get the same treatment.<br /> <br /> But not really what you were talking about though.<br /> <br /> More along those lines, there are options-<br /> <br /> 1) Mage chroniclers guide, has an option to allow even muggles to do ritual magic, although perhaps requiring reagents like a dragon's scale or the breath of a fish, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> 2) A changeling book has an option in which the local rules might change depending on which court is ascendant. If the autumn court is ascendent, changelings can start collecting secrets, up to their power stat, which they can use to use contracts they don't know, it even includes the option that possibly other supernaturals and even muggles can do the same thing.<br /> <br /> 3) Witch book for Hunter, it has it's own magic system, and even muggles can use the magic therein after buying a merit for each power they want, or casting the magic ritually.<br /> <br /> 4) Use the crafting rules from CofD book, sure only getting dice bonus is rather tame, but hey it's free magic.<br /> <br /> 5) Mirrors, forbidden lore, in which people can buy and power their magical abilities with their own sanity, for a call of cthulhu sort of deal.<br /> <br /> 6) Spirits and other supernatural beings are valid targets for supernatural merits, so hey you could have a character with a ghostly ally or a spirit contact. <br /> <br /> There might be more, but that's all I got offhand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T09:56:47-07:00","id":936597,"title":"","content":"Magic-as-Endowments. The Malleus Maleficatorum's Benedictions are essentially Catholic-flavored ritual magic. <br /> <br /> Also: the concept of \u201clesser templates\u201d has evolved since it was first introduced in <b>Second Sight</b>. These days, psychics don't qualify as a \u201clesser template\u201d anymore; they're \u201cmerely\u201d mortals with Supernatural Merits (or, at most, \u201cmicro-templates\u201d, which is another way of saying \u201ca collection of closely related Supernatural Merits\u201d). <b>Second Sight</b>'s thaumaturges only barely qualify as templates, and then only because each Tradition has a Strength and a Weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:03:09-07:00","id":936647,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about creating an Astral Mages traumaturgic tradition. Would fit pretty well because modern occult concentrates on astral a lot. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:29:18-07:00","id":936692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/936407-expanding-mortal-magic?p=936597#post936597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: the concept of \u201clesser templates\u201d has evolved since it was first introduced in <b>Second Sight</b>. These days, psychics don't qualify as a \u201clesser template\u201d anymore; they're \u201cmerely\u201d mortals with Supernatural Merits (or, at most, \u201cmicro-templates\u201d, which is another way of saying \u201ca collection of closely related Supernatural Merits\u201d). <b>Second Sight</b>'s thaumaturges only barely qualify as templates, and then only because each Tradition has a Strength and a Weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only used the word template to differentiate thaumaturges from &quot;normal mortals&quot;, not because of any mechanical implications. Although Second Sight provides the option that everyone can develop psychic powers or thaumaturgic ritual magic, it could just as well need special circumstances or an inborn trait that could be likened to a template. So even if mechanically all mortals could get supernatural merits without having to assume a mechanical template, narratively some special circumstance could still be required to develop these powers. But maybe we need another word than template to differentiate normal mortals from beings with supernatural powers, as that word already has too many connotations.<br /> <br /> I like to treat Malleus Maleficatorum's Benedictions the same way. Not everyone could just pick up a book and learn them. But I know that is not necessarily how it is presented in hunter.<br /> <br /> But I digress. Other things I thought of mortals can do:<ul><li><i>Geomancy:</i> Mortals can still shape buildings or even cities to make certain areas more conductive to specific resonances or actions. More complex geomancy, as used in ancient Irem, could also create more complex effects.</li> <li><i>Relic making:</i> In ancient Irem mortals used recipes to create relics, but even if most of those recipes got lost, dedicated mortals can still create a few relics during their lifetime.</li> <li><i>Some things just work: </i>There are some simple (or complex) rituals that a mortal can find that just work. Maybe they are powered by a supernatural patron who likes the ritual and/or gains Essence from it. Some other rituals key into the arcane physics of the world, crudely mimicking the way the God Machine works its magic.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:33:10-07:00","id":936697,"title":"","content":"You could always set up a more free-form Rituals system, where you set a dice pool, and run an extended action to do &quot;normal&quot; things in a supernatural way (such as at a distance, breaking a specific rule, or without normal tools). Like, oh say, a certain simplified psychic system I saw a while back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:50:21-07:00","id":936704,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> <br /> I've once considered the following: Within fiction, fire is a common weakness of many monsters. It is this way because it helped humanity survive in a hostile world and has become a potent symbol. What if the same reasoning was applied to the magic system? Fire wouldn't have been such a weakness had humanity never learned to use it. This would also mean that other symbols could be imbued with the same meaning. Should someone light a fire, generate electricity or create a weapon relying on their own expertise and focused effort (Willpower expenditure), and having a specific foe in mind, these assets become especially potent against entities responsive to human psyche. This includes Spirits, Ghosts, Goetia and possibly Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:54:27-07:00","id":936705,"title":"","content":"You mean <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/869141-ultra-light-psychic-powers\">this</a> psychic system? I still need to add another merit to that.<br /> <br /> Geomancy would be a pretty good expansion of the Summoning/Exorcism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T07:29:55-07:00","id":937075,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.wodcodex.com/wiki/Merits,_Thaumaturgy\" target=\"_blank\">This can give you an idea of what Thaumaturges are supposed to be able to do.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T19:13:13-07:00","id":949012,"title":"","content":"Here are some thoughts (as I mentioned, I'm kinda looking for stuff you don't need to spend Merit dots on):<br /> <br /> <b>Geomancy -</b> Uses the same modifiers as Binding/Warding, but it's an Intelligence + Occult roll. Success lets you either lower the Gauntlet penalty for ephemeral beings with appropriate Influences, or increase it for those that lack such Influences (\u00b11, probably). An exceptional success does both. Lasts until someone messes with your furniture/messes with your plants/etcetera. Indirectly bring luck by encouraging the presence of luck spirits, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Divination -</b> Use the Investigation system (use Occult in place of Investigation), and get <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/893610-random-question?p=893736#post893736\">Occult Clues</a> out of it. Maybe all failed rolls are Dramatic Failures and you only get an Incomplete Occult clue out of an ordinary success?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T19:22:08-07:00","id":949021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/936407-expanding-mortal-magic?p=949012#post949012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here are some thoughts (as I mentioned, I'm kinda looking for stuff you don't need to spend Merit dots on):<br /> <br /> <b>Geomancy -</b> Uses the same modifiers as Binding/Warding, but it's an Intelligence + Occult roll. Success lets you either lower the Gauntlet penalty for ephemeral beings with appropriate Influences, or increase it for those that lack such Influences (\u00b11, probably). An exceptional success does both. Lasts until someone messes with your furniture/messes with your plants/etcetera. Indirectly bring luck by encouraging the presence of luck spirits, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Divination -</b> Use the Investigation system (use Occult in place of Investigation), and get <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/893610-random-question?p=893736#post893736&amp;quot;]Occult</a> Clues[/URL] out of it. Maybe all failed rolls are Dramatic Failures and you only get an Incomplete Occult clue out of an ordinary success?</div> </div> </div> </div>Geomancy might be hiding in the old Chicago Workings SAS, and I think it's planned for Mummy at some point as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}